<h3>Navigating in the Carmen network editor and message windows</h3>
<p>After launching Carmen, two different windows will appear in your
screen: the CARMEN main window with a blank area for the network editor
area; and the Carmen message window where all the internal messages will
be display to confirm opening and closing networks and, mainly, it is
designed to capture all the internal messages and errors of the system.
</p>
<p><img width="425" height="324" hspace="10"
	src="../../images/screens/CARMEN main window screen.jpg"></p>
<p><img width="428" height="109" hspace="10"
	src="../../images/screens/CARMEN message window screen.jpg"></p>
<h3>Now try...</h3>
<p>To see how easy it is to add/edit/modify probabilistic nodes in
Carmen try the following steps:</p>
